#
# One rule, because the repository has one maintainer who is also its only
# collaborator. Adding per-directory rules that all name the same account would
# be maintenance with no effect: GitHub applies the last matching pattern, and
# every pattern would resolve to the same reviewer.
#
# What this file does today: GitHub requests a review from the account below on
# every pull request. What it does not do: gate the merge. Branch protection on
# `main` has "Require review from Code Owners" turned off, so the request is
# advisory until that setting is enabled. See CONTRIBUTING.md for the full set
# of protection rules currently in force.

